From 5331aefb05b2c97ab9a598f43fdde706b01a08ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomasz Wierzbicki <tomasz.wierzbicki@example.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:10:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sessions): filter the session list by host

Add a host_id filter to GET /v1/sessions and SessionsNamespace.list so
a client can ask for the sessions launched on one host instead of
paging through every session and checking host_id locally. Sessions
with no host binding are excluded.

The host binding lives on the metadata row, so the store resolves it
the way the project filter resolves membership: an IN subquery when
metadata shares the conversations database, a bounded prefetch when it
does not.

Signed-off-by: Tomasz Wierzbicki <tomasz.wierzbicki@example.com>
